  "notes": "バグる is derived from the English word \"bug\" (as in software bug). It's a verb formed by adding る to the loanword.\n\nREGISTER:\nThis is casual/colloquial language commonly used when talking about technology or figuratively about oneself. In formal contexts, use {不具合|ふぐあい}が{起|お}きる or {誤作動|ごさどう}する.\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- ～がバグる: something malfunctions\n- バグっている: to be malfunctioning (state)\n\nASPECT (ている):\nバグっている indicates an ongoing state of malfunction.",
